  "nl_text": "The rschema_0134 database is designed to manage user interactions with properties for rent. The Users table stores information about each registered user, including their email, password, phone number, unique user ID, role, and username. The Houses table contains details about available properties, such as the property's description, facilities, location, price, title, type, and publisher, linked to the user ID of the landlord who published it. The Demands table represents requests from users for specific properties, including the budget, description, location, title, type, and the user ID of the requesting party. The Orders table tracks rental agreements between users and landlords, including the lease start and end dates, order price, status, payment status, and property ID, as well as the user ID of the renter. The relationships between these tables are established through foreign keys: the Landlord_ID in the Houses table references the User_ID in the Users table, the User_ID in the Demands table references the User_ID in the Users table, and the Property_ID in the Orders table references the Property_ID in the Houses table, while the User_ID in the Orders table references the User_ID in the Users table.",
  "gold_question": "The system is a housing rental platform that includes major functions such as user management, property management, order management, and demand management. Users can register, log in, and manage their personal information on the platform. Landlords can publish property information, set property prices, types, facilities, etc., and manage and update property information. Users can post rental demands based on their needs, create orders on the platform, make payments, and manage order status. The system supports matching properties and demands, displaying property information that meets the conditions according to user needs, and providing rental services. The database design includes four main tables: Users (user table), which records basic user information; Houses (property table), which records detailed property information; Orders (order table), which records user rental orders and status; and Demands (demand table), which records user rental demands. The tables are associated through Foreign key to ensure data consistency and integrity.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_llama31/0134.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0134\nCREATE TABLE `users` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(15) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `role` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `username` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `houses` (\n  `property_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `facilities` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `location` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `landlord_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`property_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `houses_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`landlord_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `demands` (\n  `demand_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `budget` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `location` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`demand_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `demands_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `orders` (\n  `order_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `lease_start_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `lease_end_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `order_price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `payment_status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `property_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`order_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `orders_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`property_id`) REFERENCES `houses` (`property_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `orders_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
